nces, docs:check-links, check:doc-examples and check:doc-example-ids all 0; check-governed-queue-guard --test over 12 paths 0, NOT GOVERNED. pnpm --filter @object-ui/types lint exit 0, 0 errors, and no warning on an added line (eslint json over the 10 touched files). Ablations, committed first, each run through objectstack's scripts/ablation-replace.mjs (anchor hit, blob moved, restore proven blob==HEAD with git diff HEAD empty). The subject is imported from src by relative path, so no dist build was involved. A1 deleted zod FormFieldSchema.multiple: predicted 2 red + tsc red, measured 2 red / 34 green, tsc -p tsconfig.test.json exit 2. A2 deleted zod FormSchema.showSubmit: predicted 2 red + tsc red, measured 2 red / 34 green, tsc exit 2. A3 renamed zod ObjectKanbanSchema.dataSource away: predicted 1 red + tsc red, measured 1 red / 35 green, tsc exit 2. M3 before/after: the scratch port (never committed) of #11069's findUndeclaredKeys over the shipped strict face on the M1 corpora read, at base 88fbd793d, 588 docs, 158 strict-refused / 120 strict-only, class (ii) 32/149/141; at head 5a63e4ab5, 588, 102/64, class (ii) 19/48/44. Class (iii) 10/15/13 and class (i) 47/69/49 did not move. The tolerant face refused the same 38 documents at both commits. Runtime probe (scratch vitest, never committed): the real SchemaRenderer with @object-ui/fields registered rendered each corpus document with and without each form key. Markup DIFFERS for showSubmit, multiple (file, image), rows, accept, dimensions, min, max, minLength, maxLength and pattern. It is SAME for format, validation.message and min_length, and for multiple on the built-in select. NOT MEASURED: the Spec Main Shape Gate (needs an @objectstack/spec main build; declared to CI) and the repository-wide lint (CI's run).",
